          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Eifersucht",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Eifersucht — \"jealousy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Seine Eifersucht macht seine Freundin traurig. His jealousy makes his girlfriend sad."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No plural in everyday use. The adjective is eifersüchtig — jealous."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Eifersucht is built on Eifer \"zeal, eagerness\" and Sucht \"sickness, craving\"; Sucht is inherited from Old High German suht, from Proto-Germanic suhtiz (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
